title: Windows Hello is usable by apps on the founder's laptop (pre-P02)
summary: 'The founder has a Windows Hello PIN. dsregcmd''s NgcSet:NO is only the Windows Hello for Business flag. UserConsentVerifier reports Available and KeyCredentialManager.IsSupportedAsync is true, which unblocks W4 phase B. Next: probe P02, an ECDSA P-256 key in the Microsoft Passport (NGC) KSP that signs only after a Hello gesture.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#identity'
  - '#gnomon-helper'
learnings:
  - dsregcmd NgcSet tracks Windows Hello for Business, not the consumer Hello PIN; check UserConsentVerifier.CheckAvailabilityAsync / KeyCredentialManager.IsSupportedAsync instead
